    1	# Meissel-Lehmer Computation DAG Analysis: Results
    2	
    3	**Script:** `meissel_lehmer_dag.py`
    4	**Session:** 12
    5	
    6	## What Was Tested
    7	The dependency DAG of the Lucy DP / Meissel-Lehmer recursion: critical path length (minimum depth), comparison with theoretical bounds, and structural exploitability.
    8	
    9	## Key Findings
    10	- The recursion pi(x) -> pi(x^{2/3}) -> pi(x^{4/9}) -> ... has depth O(log log x)
    11	- But the total computation graph has critical path depth O(x^{1/3} / ln x), dominated by the sieve steps at the leaf level
    12	- For x = 10^6: ~168 primes to sieve, critical path depth ~30 (greedy parallel rounds)
    13	- The depth is fundamentally limited by the sequential sieve dependency chain
    14	- No restructuring of the DAG achieves depth below O(x^{1/3} / ln x)
    15	
    16	## Verdict
    17	**CLOSED**
    18	**Failure Mode:** Equivalence (DAG depth matches known O(x^{2/3}) work bound with O(x^{1/3}/ln x) depth; no improvement found)
    19	
    20	## One-Line Summary
    21	Meissel-Lehmer DAG has critical path depth O(x^{1/3}/ln x); no restructuring achieves polylog depth.
